{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>If he curse his Elohim, and bear his sin.</b> There is nothing here but bearing of sin — that is, the matter hangs between him and his Maker, a doubtful capital case to be lenient with, for perhaps he did not intend it toward HaShem but only toward the judges, since judges are called 'elohim.' And one need not investigate the intent of the person who curses with the name Elohim. But one who pronounces the name YHWH — that which Scripture specifies as the special name — shall surely be put to death."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:54.621274046Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}